n) (assoc rows address row))))))\n367-      (let [tree {:root root :rows rows}]\n368-        (when-let [defect (vm/validate-rows tree)]\n369-          (throw (ex-info \"Invalid canonical row closure\" {:rule :verifier/tree :defect defect})))\n370-        tree))))\n371-\n372-\n373-(defn check-replay-root!\n374-  \"Refuse if a newly compiled replay does not name the retained root.\"\n375-  [fixture replayed-ast expected-root]\n376-  (when-not (and (jing/segment-address? expected-root)\n377-                 (= expected-root (:root (vm/ast->semantic-bytecode replayed-ast))))\n378-    (throw (ex-info \"Recompiled root differs from retained root\"\n379-                    {:rule :verifier/fixture :fixture fixture :stage :root})))\n380-  true)\n                  (throw (ex-info \"content bytes are not strict Base64\"\n                                  {:address address\n                                   :reason :base64}))))]\n    (when-not (segment-bytes-match? address bs)\n      (throw (ex-info \"content address does not match payload hash\"\n                      {:address address, :reason :hash-mismatch})))\n    (try (cbor/decode bs)\n         (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default) _\n           (throw (ex-info \"content payload is not one canonical payload\"\n                           {:address address, :reason :non-canonical}))))\n    bs))\n\n\n(defn materialize!\n  \"Content-address payload and store it through the handle's byte store.\n\n   Supports [handle payload] (defaulting to default-hash-algorithm, :blake3)\n   and [handle payload {:keys [algorithm]}].\n\n   The payload is encoded exactly once. The address is derived solely from\n   those canonical bytes, and the same bytes go to the backend effect\n   :put-bytes-fn as (put-bytes-fn address bytes). The backend must answer\n   with one of:\n\n     :inserted -- the bytes are durably stored now;\n     :present  -- bytes are already stored under that address.\n\n   Any other answer is an invalid backend result and throws: DaoJing does\n   not accept ambiguous truthiness. The address is returned only after the\n   backend reports success.\n\n   On :present the stored bytes are read back through :get-bytes-fn and\n   verified both by hash against the address and byte for byte against the\n   proposed bytes. Equal content is idempotent and returns the same\n   address. Content that does not hash to its own address is an integrity\n   failure and throws loudly. Nothing is ever overwritten.\"\n  ([handle payload]\n   (materialize! handle payload {:algorithm default-hash-algorithm}))\n  ([handle payload opts]\n   (let [put (:put-bytes-fn handle)\n         get-fn (:get-bytes-fn handle)]\n     (when-not (fn? put)\n       (throw (ex-info \"dao.jing handle requires :put-bytes-fn\"\n                       {:handle handle})))\n     (when-not (fn? get-fn)\n       (throw (ex-info \"dao.jing handle requires :get-bytes-fn\"\n                       {:handle handle})))\n     (let [algo (clojure.core/get opts :algorithm default-hash-algorithm)\n           reg (clojure.core/get registry algo)]\n       (when-not reg\n         (throw (ex-info (str \"unsupported hash algorithm: \" algo)\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md:257:The two delivery states of §1.1 are the states at which the evaluator parks by itself. They are special cases of its general state between any two instructions, `⟨A, pc, W↾L(pc), E, K⟩`, which `vm-hot` materializes whenever fuel runs out (`semantic.cljc:142-143`) and which the carrier expresses as the `run` state of §1.2. A step is atomic: effects are observed only inside a step or inside the scheduler's sweep, so no state between steps holds a half-issued effect; atomicity of a step is not transactionality of the outside world (an append performed before a host exception is not undone). A task is a **product**: at most one active activation (the `run`), its ordered pending waits, its ordered completed wakes (the ready queue: a woken wait with the value, status and cursor update its effect produced, carried by the `:ready` row of §2.3), its parked table, and its stores. The scheduler constructs every combination: resuming one of several woken waits leaves the others queued and the unresolved ones pending (`engine.cljc:2294-2312`, `:2305`). Every such state is **representable**. The lift refuses only what is not **portable** (a value with no wire form), not **satisfied** (code or dependencies the receiver lacks), or a **hold** (a driver-internal observation in flight: §7.1 step 1), never a pc. The static correspondence of §4 holds at every pc of a body: distinct virtuals in `L(p) ∪ def(p)` hold distinct physical registers (`derive/allocation`), and the stack kernel's operand region at A pc `p` is `stack-layout(p) ++ uses(p)` above a dead prefix (§4.3); both are checks (§5.6), not theorems. A root whose task has an active activation has kind `:running` (§2.6) and is a custody subject like a blocked or parked root (§7.3).\ndocs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md:2985:| D1 | §5.5 | positions carry identities; the renaming operation, injective correspondence, separate descriptor equivalence and five negative controls; three distinct lanes asserted per case | engineer D1, codex F4, M11 and M12 survived, probe 4 |\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat > /tmp/d1-r14-subset.clj <<'EOF'\n(require '[dao.jing :as jing] '[yin.repl.store :as file] '[yang.correspondence-batch :as batch] '[yang.correspondence-verifier :as v] '[clojure.pprint :as pp])\n(let [progress (batch/read-progress \\\"target/d1-r9b-outcomes.edn\\\")\n      outcomes (:outcomes progress)\n      maxima (into {} (for [[label f] [[:storage :storage-bytes] [:sites :sites] [:pre-stamp #(get-in % [:rows :pre-stamp])] [:stamped #(get-in % [:rows :stamped])]]]\n                        [label (key (apply max-key (comp f val) outcomes))]))\n      ids (set (vals maxima))\n      src (file/open {:type :file :dir \\\"target/d1-r9b-store\\\"})\n      dst (file/open {:type :file :dir \\\"test/yang/latte_oracle/slice9_correspondence_store\\\"})]\n  (try\n    (let [entries (into {} (for [id ids\n                                 :let [o (get outcomes id) addresses (:addresses o)\n                                       trees (mapv #(v/fetch-tree\"'! src (addresses %) 100000) [:root :stamped-root])]]\n                             (do\n                               (doseq [[_ address] addresses]\n                                 (when-not (= address (jing/materialize! dst (jing/get src address ::missing)))\n                                   (throw (ex-info \"Direct address mismatch\" {:id id :address address}))))\n                               (doseq [tree trees [_ row] (:rows tree)]\n                                 (when-not (= (first row) (jing/materialize! dst (subvec row 1)))\n                                   (throw (ex-info \"Row address mismatch\" {:id id :row (first row)}))))\n                               [id (select-keys o [:admission-origin :addresses :rows :sites :storage-bytes])])))]\n      (spit \"test/yang/latte_oracle/slice9_correspondence_store/manifest.edn\"\n            (with-out-str (pp/pprint {:version 1 :scope :selected-static-fixture-closures :selection :observed-corpus-maxima :maxima maxima :fixtures entries :full-corpus-retention-owner :pending :open-procedure :copy-directory-to-scratch-before-open :excludes [:recipe :image-derivations :instruction-provenance :lane-traces] :source-outcomes-sha256 \"bd0e7e113a2e10a80f26402443c2f18be7cc2701e7261077b7e0772c55acda39\"})))\n      (prn {:maxima maxima :fixtures ids}))\n    (finally (file/close! dst) (file/close! src))))\nEOF\njava -Xmx4g -cp \"$(clojure -Spath -A:test)\" clojure.main /tmp/d1-r14-subset.clj'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
